m{g}$ |\n| Milligram | $\\textrm{mg}$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of mass is $\\textrm{mg}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198065 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12511" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198065 #edb/ref 1071 "A melon has a mass of $1\\,\\textrm{kg}.$ What is this mass in grams?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198065 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8783fe1f-5b08-5862-9e3d-231ba39ad4e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198065 #edb/ref 1074 "A table showing the metric units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilogram | $\\textrm{kg}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{kg} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\textrm{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\textrm{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mg} = 1\\,\\textrm{g}$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\textrm{kg}$ is equivalent to $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{g}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198068 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198068 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we want to measure the mass of a flat-screen TV. Which of the following customary units could we use?\n\nI. $\\textrm{yd}$\n\nII. $\\textrm{ft}$\n\nIII. $\\textrm{lb}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198068 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0526feee-cfe1-5aa2-9de0-a37e7a162492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198068 #edb/ref 1074 "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\textrm{ton}$ |\n| Pound | $\\textrm{lb}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\textrm{oz}$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of mass is $\\textrm{lb}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198069 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12517" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198069 #edb/ref 1071 "An american bison has a mass of $1\\,\\textrm{ton}.$ What is this mass in pounds?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198069 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16c47009-d38d-5957-bc2d-525483e18161" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198069 #edb/ref 1074 "A table showing the customary units of mass is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ton | $\\textrm{ton}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{ton} = 2,000\\,\\textrm{lb}$ |\n| Pound | $\\textrm{lb}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{lb} = 16\\,\\textrm{oz}$ |\n| Ounce | $\\textrm{oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, $1\\,\\textrm{ton}$ is equivalent to $2,000\\,\\textrm{lb}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Metric Units of Mass" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198422 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "666d43f8-bf05-51b0-af1f-d89540f4c29c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1039 "Stating Mass Conversions in Metric Units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198423 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e01d9e5b-d4e5-5e84-84c5-33f6678b53ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198426 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198426 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198426 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 175921864316